WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:05.430
It almost goes without saying that the inner
workings of the SCP Foundation are kept secret

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.390
from the general population.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:12.019
Your average Joe doesn’t need or want to
know about the terrifying entities and bizarre

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:17.589
experiments happening behind the closed doors
of the various Foundation research sites.

00:00:17.589 --> 00:00:24.050
But there are some secrets of the SCP Foundation
that even its own staff know very little about.

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:31.009
One such mystery is the highly classified
and immensely powerful O5-Council, or Overwatch

00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:35.719
Council, that oversees everything that goes
on within the SCP Foundation.

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:40.750
They are considered the highest authority
within the organization, but very little is

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:42.250
known about them.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:47.579
In fact, according to one official report
in the SCP Foundation archives, the O5 Council

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:49.739
does not exist at all.

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:50.989
Stick with me, here.

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:55.660
There are decades of reports concerning the
Council, there is a wealth of historical evidence

00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:02.089
pointing to their existence and influence,
but they do not definitely exist.

00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:04.199
At least, they don’t right now.

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:10.340
Take a deep breath, try and untangle the knots
we just tied in your brain, sit back and listen.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:16.820
This is the story of SCP-001, the O5 Council
itself.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:23.400
In 1965, SCP Foundation Administrator William
Cohen was preparing to leave his position.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.810
To prepare his successor, H.V.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:30.950
Oleander, Administrator Cohen drafted a series
of letters intended to pass on important,

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.920
and highly guarded knowledge, to the man who
would take his place.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.310
In the letter, Administrator Cohen explained
that he was retiring early for a specific

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:45.670
reason, writing, “A tar clings to my mind,
sticking to every neuron and slowing my every

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:46.670
thought.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.680
In truth, I am unwell.”
Cohen’s decline had begun eight years prior,

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:57.000
in late 1957 after the launch of Soviet space
probe Sputnik-1 into the Earth’s orbit.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.090
The Foundation’s interest had been drawn
to the probe after a foreign signal had been

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.840
detected trying to communicate with it.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:09.179
Not a signal from a foreign nation, mind you,
but something from much further away, and

00:02:09.179 --> 00:02:12.120
likely something that was not human.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.250
Whatever it was, it was trying to communicate,
and it was getting closer.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:23.310
On January 4, 1958, the signal stopped and
an unidentified object arrived on Earth.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:28.159
Cohen was summoned to the war room at Site-00,
much to his surprise.

00:02:28.159 --> 00:02:31.810
It was highly unusual for guests to be invited
to the Site.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:36.650
There, they worked together to identify the
nature of the situation with Sputnik, until

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:42.879
a single burst of gamma radiation was detected
and Sputnik’s orbit began to decay.

00:02:42.879 --> 00:02:47.569
The Council panicked, calling heads of state
and calling for as many resources as possible.

00:02:47.569 --> 00:02:52.129
They had worked themselves into a frenzy and
were planning to shoot down the first space

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:54.180
probe in Earth’s history.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:03:00.170
Eventually, the decision was placed in Cohen’s
hands: let the probe land on its own, or shoot

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:01.420
it down?

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:06.329
Overwhelmed by the Council’s intensity,
Cohen told them to do what they thought was

00:03:06.329 --> 00:03:07.329
best.

00:03:07.329 --> 00:03:08.329
They shot it down.

00:03:08.329 --> 00:03:11.709
He did not want to, but he crumbled under
the pressure.

00:03:11.709 --> 00:03:18.219
There were so many of them and only one of
him, and they seemed so certain in their decision.

00:03:18.219 --> 00:03:22.739
This was the first decision in his career
that Cohen regretted, and it was presumably

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:24.610
followed by many more.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:29.230
He continued in his letter, saying, “And
now what credibility do I have left to disagree

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.230
with them?

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.500
I am but a mouthpiece.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:37.069
A sad, old puppet tangled up and caught in
the very strings used to make him dance.”

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:42.269
Cohen wrote his letter to his successor with
one warning: “Just as I have shown you vulnerability

00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:47.159
here in the hopes I might gain your trust,
please consider asking the same from those

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:49.529
who would insist you trust them.”

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:55.459
In March of 1958, following the incident with
Sputnik, the O5 Council collectively submitted

00:03:55.459 --> 00:03:58.319
a notice to the Foundation’s Leadership
Committee.

00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:03.980
They stated simply: “The Individual you
call your administrator has proven insufficient.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:08.139
We solicit you to make your preparations and
nominate another.”

00:04:08.139 --> 00:04:12.629
No individual members of the Council wrote
in, but rather submitted their thoughts as

00:04:12.629 --> 00:04:17.290
a collective, as if thinking together as one
single mind.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:23.430
The language used was also curious, saying
“Your Administrator,” rather than “Our

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:24.430
Administrator.”

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:29.750
The O5 Council seemed to think of itself as
something separate from the SCP Foundation,

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:35.480
its own entity rather than simply a powerful
arm or leader of the organization itself.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:39.870
On June 11, 1962, another notice was sent
out.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:45.670
It read, “Foundation, a life lived in service
of the greater good is invalidated if death

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.530
does not also serve.”

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:55.370
On November 11, 1965, a third notice was sent
out, this time to all Foundation staff: “Please

00:04:55.370 --> 00:05:00.280
join us in remembering the life and career
of Administrator William Cohen.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:03.040
The only constant is change.

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:09.530
Because of this, the erosion of his skills,
abilities, knowledge, and confidence was inevitable.”

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:10.530
Administrator H.V.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:14.400
Oleander took over the position for many years
after Cohen’s demise.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:21.540
In 1988, he prepared to step down and drafted
a letter to his successor, Natalia Elllingbrooke.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:26.630
Like Cohen before him, Oleander tried his
best to explain where he went wrong, in the

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:28.890
hope that she might do better.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:32.540
Oleander began the letter, “I used to have
such an ego.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:37.780
This job, this life, and the burdens that
surround it crush and squeeze you until all

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:40.610
you have left is what they force you to keep.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:45.110
My mind and my soul feel as though they've
been contorted into the shape of someone I

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.970
no longer recognize.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:53.260
My predecessor, may he rest in peace, described
his years as if he were trapped behind smoky

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:56.880
glass and made to watch a foggy world pass
him by.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.430
Like some sort of voyeur.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:03.830
I, too, feel imprisoned but I realize that
it was never a looking glass.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:06.000
It is a mirror.”

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.740
The events detailed in the letter began in
November of 1985, after a powerful storm had

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:16.970
ripped through New England and caused severe
damage to Site-31’s power grid.

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:22.360
During the power outage, a multi-stage containment
breach occurred and an unnamed infovore escaped

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.740
from the facility.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:29.750
The entity was lost until March of 1986, when
it was detected in a government facility in

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:31.190
Warsaw, Poland.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:35.580
Determined to make up for his previous failure,
Oleander organized a mission to bring the

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.970
entity back into custody.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:42.100
His team tracked it down and was prepared
to apprehend the entity’s host when the

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:47.020
O5 Council expressed concern that this behavior
might cause an international incident and

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:48.020
intervened.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:52.320
The Council made the decision to reach out
to local and international governments in

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.120
Poland, allowing the entity to escape to Pripyat,
Ukraine.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:07:00.500
Oleander and the Council went head to head
on this, pushing and pulling and becoming

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.270
increasingly aggressive on either side.

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:08.370
Oleander could not make up his mind about
what to do: listen to the Council, or trust

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.470
his own gut?

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:17.110
On April 26, 1986, his indecision resulted
in a nuclear disaster in Soviet territory.

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:21.140
Not only that, but the entity still evaded
containment.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.860
The mission was a complete failure.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:28.500
The O5 Council submitted a report on the incident,
stating: “We recommended that the healing

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:31.750
process commence by first assigning blame.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:35.400
The collective good would be served by purging
liability.”

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:37.800
And “WE WOULD HAVE HELPED.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:38.800
ANYONE WOULD HAVE HELPED.

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:40.090
WHY DENY IT??”

00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:42.850
By now, the pattern has probably become clear
to you.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:48.370
The Administrator and the Council fall into
conflict over a difficult decision.

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:49.770
Something goes horribly wrong.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:54.330
A new Administrator is chosen, the former
Administrator writes them a letter to prepare

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:58.900
them for the heavy demands of the job, and
the cycle begins again.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:03.470
As you might expect, during those days of
her administration, Oleander’s replacement

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:09.000
Natalie Ellingbrooke sat down to write a letter
of warning to one Michelle Wilkes, who was

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:11.170
chosen to replace her.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:15.620
Ellingbrooke began her letter, “As you've
likely surmised from our few meetings, I walk

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.610
with a pronounced limp and favor my left leg.

00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:23.210
How I came to be like this isn't especially
interesting but what it did to me might be

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:26.320
of interest to a person in your position.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:30.020
Any man or woman changes when they are exposed
to pain.

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:32.550
Simply put, it has to go somewhere.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:36.899
If you hold it all within yourself, it may
stay contained but it will surely destroy

00:08:36.899 --> 00:08:39.029
you when you've had your fill.

00:08:39.029 --> 00:08:44.649
It festers in all the spaces you let it occupy,
warping and scarring what used to be healthy,

00:08:44.649 --> 00:08:46.610
happy tissue sat beneath.

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:48.800
Some people have hobbies, but me?

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:50.279
I've always just had my work.

00:08:50.279 --> 00:08:54.360
I've been ringside for so much pain in my
time with the Foundation.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:59.470
My predecessor left me a note, much like I
am leaving you, and in it he warned me of

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:03.279
the tremendous duty and guilt he hid in order
to do his job.

00:09:03.279 --> 00:09:08.511
Although the slings and arrows of outrageous
fortune stung him quite keenly, I assure you

00:09:08.511 --> 00:09:11.040
I have suffered every bit his equal.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:15.970
The breach at the Olympics in '94, losing
control of Site-248 in '96.

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:19.069
Botched facility transfer of Hong Kong in
'97.

00:09:19.069 --> 00:09:20.899
Bombings in Bali in '02.

00:09:20.899 --> 00:09:24.029
The dispute with ORIA in the Congo in '03.

00:09:24.029 --> 00:09:26.220
The GOC Ultimatum in '04.”

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:31.009
She continued, “Although I have weathered
much, my tenure is up not with the sort of

00:09:31.009 --> 00:09:36.019
precipitating bang that ousted Oleander, but
rather the quiet whimper of stepping away

00:09:36.019 --> 00:09:39.019
from a battle I no longer wish to fight.

00:09:39.019 --> 00:09:43.860
I am tired of the Council calling a meeting
on every decision I try to make and I am tired

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:47.230
of calling one on every decision they try
to make without me.

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:51.230
I guess that reasoning is another tribute
to the selfish life I have led.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:55.249
My ideal way to say goodbye would have been
to simply stop coming in.

00:09:55.249 --> 00:10:00.220
My desk would have sat empty, emails unread,
until one day a courier showed up with my

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:01.830
keys and badge.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:08.180
But even here, at the end of my career, the
O5 Council insists on refusing to let me be

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:09.420
myself.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:14.759
So tomorrow I will play the part of a dutiful
officer resigning her post and walk away from

00:10:14.759 --> 00:10:20.310
Site-00 with my head held high and those overbearing
bastards in the rear-view mirror.

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:24.699
I pray that your head will never be so bowed
as mine has.”

00:10:24.699 --> 00:10:29.270
Administrator Wilkes took her predecessor’s
words to heart and began her tenure with a

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.610
new proposal for Project TETHYS.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:36.540
The project would include modifications to
the Three Gorges Dam facility at the Yangtze

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:44.720
River, as part of a containment procedure
for Entity 2005-C-ET-011.

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:47.899
The Council refused to approve her proposal.

00:10:47.899 --> 00:10:52.170
Administrator Wilkes insisted that they provide
a list of concerns, explaining what their

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:54.360
issues with her proposal were.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:58.990
The two argued back and forth over the necessity
of a meeting until the Council submitted this

00:10:58.990 --> 00:11:03.220
note to her: “We know how important it is
to get off on the right foot.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:08.509
Although This Body respects you and the autonomy
which you command, We have also seen many

00:11:08.509 --> 00:11:09.639
come and go.

00:11:09.639 --> 00:11:14.990
You were chosen from your peers but they have
chosen many others in the past.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:17.050
We remain unconvinced.

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:22.100
Before you, Ellingbrooke, who spent her whole
life pushing others aside so she could lead.

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:24.329
She left all others behind.

00:11:24.329 --> 00:11:27.940
Trees with no roots do not hold to the ground.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:33.089
Before her, Oleander, who wanted so much to
be seen as your Hero in white.

00:11:33.089 --> 00:11:37.519
He could no longer live with himself once
his clothes were stained, but The Sin does

00:11:37.519 --> 00:11:39.529
not define The Saint.

00:11:39.529 --> 00:11:44.120
Before him, Cohen, who wanted nothing more
than to be the one who made the decisions.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:48.129
He collapsed in on himself when there was
no easy victory.

00:11:48.129 --> 00:11:49.910
No man is an island.

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:53.970
And a dozen more whose names We have subrogated.

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:55.420
You need Us.

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:58.829
You are not enough.”

00:11:58.829 --> 00:12:04.149
Administrator Wilkes was offended by this
response and argued that the meeting was unnecessary.

00:12:04.149 --> 00:12:09.060
She asked for the Council to trust her expertise
and the expertise of her employees.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:14.160
They responded, “Your distinctiveness did
not arise from the ether; You are a synthesis

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.459
of available materials and experiences.

00:12:17.459 --> 00:12:20.209
If needed, another could be synthesized.

00:12:20.209 --> 00:12:22.029
We are needed.

00:12:22.029 --> 00:12:24.190
We are necessary.

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:25.800
We synthesize.

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:27.010
You are not.

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:28.519
You cannot.

00:12:28.519 --> 00:12:31.290
Become We or become They.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:33.509
The choice is yours.”

00:12:33.509 --> 00:12:35.760
Administrator Wilkes suddenly understood.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:39.939
The Council was not a part of the Foundation,
they were something else entirely.

00:12:39.939 --> 00:12:44.999
Though she couldn’t be completely sure what
they were, she knew one thing for certain:

00:12:44.999 --> 00:12:47.300
they were not her friends.

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:50.839
She fired back at the Council’s threats:
“You cast your shadow over the future with

00:12:50.839 --> 00:12:55.450
your threats and intimidation, certain we
would be nothing without you, but I am forced

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:59.110
to wonder who or what would you be without
us?

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:03.660
I stand with the countless thousands that
have died for our mission, the people that

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:08.709
have engineered our solutions, the people
that will build them, and the people that

00:13:08.709 --> 00:13:15.120
will risk their lives in order to carry out
these procedures in the hope our mission might

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:17.499
one day be complete.

00:13:17.499 --> 00:13:19.779
Without them, I know I would be nothing.

00:13:19.779 --> 00:13:22.430
We are willing to take our chances without
you.

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:25.259
I am going to offer you the same choice you
gave me.

00:13:25.259 --> 00:13:27.309
Become We or become They.”

00:13:27.309 --> 00:13:31.819
Several days passed with no response, and
Administrator Wilkes made the most difficult

00:13:31.819 --> 00:13:37.430
decision of her career: She suspended the
appointment of the O5 Council until a day

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:40.420
comes when it becomes necessary again.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:44.910
Secure Area-00 has been set up around the
area containing SCP-001.

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:50.839
The area has been classified, designated Level
6 or Cosmic Secret.

00:13:50.839 --> 00:13:55.829
The coordinates of this Secure Area are stored
in cranial implants placed in 15 carefully

00:13:55.829 --> 00:14:01.230
selected Foundation leaders, including Ethics
Committee members and Site Directors.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:05.550
These candidates can participate in voting
once a vote is called, but are to be kept

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:09.220
unaware of their status as voters unless it
becomes necessary.

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:14.329
If a supermajority votes to decrypt the contents
of these cranial implants, the location of

00:14:14.329 --> 00:14:17.509
Secure Area-00 will be revealed to them.

00:14:17.509 --> 00:14:23.040
If the security of these implants becomes
compromised, COGITA.aic will generate a new

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:26.660
protocol and a new list of candidates will
be selected.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:31.420
The original candidates will have the encrypted
information deleted from their minds.

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:37.830
No one may access Secure Area-00 at any time
for any reason unless the aforementioned vote

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:39.279
takes place.

00:14:39.279 --> 00:14:45.040
Operation protocols, defenses, building schematics,
and all other information about the Site have

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:47.449
been expunged from Foundation records.

00:14:47.449 --> 00:14:49.199
Oh, what’s this?

00:14:49.199 --> 00:14:52.040
A new Addendum has been unlocked!

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:54.040
This is for your eyes and ears only.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.540
Yes, I’m talking to you.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.810
Do not share this information with anyone
else.

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:04.160
A retinal scan has confirmed your identity
and the COGITO protocol has been executed.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:09.529
You are receiving this Addendum because Administrator
Michelle Wilkes is dead, after nearly twenty

00:15:09.529 --> 00:15:11.259
years of service.

00:15:11.259 --> 00:15:14.779
Before her death, she prepared a statement
regarding the role of the Administrator at

00:15:14.779 --> 00:15:15.870
the Foundation.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:22.259
The Addendum contains a message from Administrator
Michelle Wilkes, to you, her designated successor.

00:15:22.259 --> 00:15:27.389
Surprise, you have been chosen as the next
Administrator for The SCP Foundation.

00:15:27.389 --> 00:15:30.290
You may be surprised, asking “Really, me?”

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:31.790
Yes, you.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:36.459
You may not know it, but you were chosen quite
some time ago.

00:15:36.459 --> 00:15:39.410
The cranial implant has been in place for
years.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.540
Now it is ready to be activated.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:45.629
Michelle Wilkes’s message is intended to
prepare you for the trials and tribulations

00:15:45.629 --> 00:15:51.339
that lie ahead, and to encourage you to ask
yourself: what kind of leader will you be?

00:15:51.339 --> 00:15:55.759
Are you willing to do whatever it takes to
perform this most solemn duty?

00:15:55.759 --> 00:15:58.620
The following comes from the former Administrator
herself.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:02.300
Listen carefully, and consider what she has
to say.

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:07.101
Your future at the Foundation, the fate of
your subordinates, and your very legacy, may

00:16:07.101 --> 00:16:08.399
depend on it.

00:16:08.399 --> 00:16:13.540
“Consider now, before fate takes away the
luxury of time, what type of person, co-worker,

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.559
and leader you want to be.

00:16:15.559 --> 00:16:20.249
Each and every one of the Administrators before
me was challenged in terms both great and

00:16:20.249 --> 00:16:24.430
small during their tenures, and I was no exception
to this pattern.

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:28.179
The office you occupy is not about the power
and influence you now command.

00:16:28.179 --> 00:16:32.829
Nor is it even about the unfathomable responsibility
you must now shepherd.

00:16:32.829 --> 00:16:37.559
It is instead about the character, integrity,
and vision with which you meet the test of

00:16:37.559 --> 00:16:41.519
leadership and, should you prove worthy, surmount
it.

00:16:41.519 --> 00:16:46.129
You and the people you will lead must be asked
to undertake tasks no person should ever be

00:16:46.129 --> 00:16:47.379
asked to carry out.

00:16:47.379 --> 00:16:52.220
Yet duty and the safety of all mankind demand
that you make this sacrifice.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:53.220
For them.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:54.220
For each other.

00:16:54.220 --> 00:16:58.730
If your resolve should ever falter, know that
everyone you lead stands with you.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:02.759
We are ready to follow you into the blackest
night if you let us believe in the promise

00:17:02.759 --> 00:17:03.759
of dawn.

00:17:03.759 --> 00:17:06.929
But should your resolve ever break, the Council
awaits.

00:17:06.929 --> 00:17:09.970
They will invite you to Site-00 if you ask.

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:11.839
You need only surrender.

00:17:11.839 --> 00:17:14.039
Best wishes, M. Wilkes.

00:17:14.039 --> 00:17:15.039
Former Administrator.”

00:17:15.039 --> 00:17:18.549
What, exactly, is the O5 Council?

00:17:18.549 --> 00:17:21.440
That is a question not easily answered.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:27.650
They are not flesh and blood, not individual
minds and feelings, but something else entirely.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:34.620
They are a collective, something that thinks,
breathes, and votes together as one being.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:39.149
They view the world as two things: We, and
They.

00:17:39.149 --> 00:17:43.760
As you prepare to take on the role of Administrator,
keep in mind who you are.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:50.810
Be strong, be brave, be resolute, and hold
on to your sense of right and wrong.

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:56.350
But if you ever should falter, if you decide
to stop being You and become We, there is

00:17:56.350 --> 00:17:57.840
always Site-00.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:03.929
Remember, even though they do not officially
exist: the Council awaits.

00:18:03.929 --> 00:18:10.559
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The Gate Guardian”
and “SCP-001 - The Black Moon” for more

00:18:10.559 --> 00:18:12.850
enigmatic SCP-001 proposals!

